WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.719 --> 00:00:05.370
Riddle us this: who's an actor that's already
played one comic book bad guy and could be

00:00:05.370 --> 00:00:09.980
making the leap from Marvel Studios to the
DC Extended Universe to play a Batman villain?

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:14.260
According to We Got This Covered, Chiwetel
Ejiofor, who played the villainous Mordo in

00:00:14.260 --> 00:00:19.140
Doctor Strange, is in consideration to play
the Riddler in director Matt Reeves' The Batman.

00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:23.320
The upcoming flick will purportedly feature
a bevy of baddies for Batman to face.

00:00:23.560 --> 00:00:28.000
It's expected that the Riddler, whose given
name is Edward Nygma, a play on the word "enigma,"

00:00:28.020 --> 00:00:30.320
will be included in the film's slew of villains.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:32.800
"Oh...Bruce Wayne!"

00:00:33.020 --> 00:00:34.480
"No, that's my name.

00:00:34.980 --> 00:00:35.640
And you are?"

00:00:35.960 --> 00:00:36.700
"Nygma.

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:37.780
Edward.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:39.280
Edward Nygma."

00:00:39.400 --> 00:00:43.600
We Got This Covered claims that The Batman
will include "at least six or seven" supercrooks

00:00:43.600 --> 00:00:47.190
for the Dark Knight to vanquish, with the
Riddler being "all but confirmed" for one

00:00:47.190 --> 00:00:49.700
of the more prominent positions in the rogues
gallery.

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:54.440
The Riddler is the brainchild of writer Bill
Finger and artist Dick Sprang, first appearing

00:00:54.440 --> 00:00:57.400
in Detective Comics #140 in 1948.

00:00:57.760 --> 00:01:02.700
A criminal mastermind who relishes in complex
riddles and has a flair for the dramatic,

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:06.920
leaving clues at crime scenes for Gotham City
authorities to find and often boasting about

00:01:06.920 --> 00:01:11.960
his genius-level intellect, the Riddler is
intensely competitive and obsessed with puzzles.

00:01:12.150 --> 00:01:15.760
When the Riddler learned that he could get
away with cheating at games, he started a

00:01:15.760 --> 00:01:20.560
life of crime, donning a green, black and
purple costume littered with question marks,

00:01:20.560 --> 00:01:24.670
cheating people out of money and pride, and
styling himself as an enemy of Batman, whom

00:01:24.670 --> 00:01:27.280
he deemed to be a worthy opponent in mental
combat.

00:01:27.729 --> 00:01:32.060
The mere thought of Ejiofor, who was nominated
for an Oscar for his performance in 12 Years

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:35.460
a Slave, taking on the role of the Riddler
is worth getting excited about.

00:01:35.700 --> 00:01:39.780
But by We Got This Covered's own admission,
it might not actually happen, for a couple

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:40.300
reasons.

00:01:40.620 --> 00:01:45.100
Reportedly, Ejiofor is just one of a number
of actors Warner Bros. is said to be eyeing

00:01:45.100 --> 00:01:48.810
to play the Riddler in The Batman, though
it's unclear as of this writing who else the

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:50.460
studio is sizing up for the role.

00:01:50.600 --> 00:01:54.640
Additionally, if Ejiofor doesn't end up landing
the role of the Riddler, word is that he'll

00:01:54.640 --> 00:01:55.840
secure a different gig.

00:01:56.170 --> 00:02:00.560
We Got This Covered's report claims that Warner
Bros. has Ejiofor in mind for several different

00:02:00.560 --> 00:02:06.190
roles, including famous Batman adversary Two-Face
and longtime Wayne family ally Lucius Fox.

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:07.800
"Didn't you get the memo?"

00:02:07.980 --> 00:02:12.500
It seems plausible that Ejiofor will be involved
in The Batman in some capacity, likely as

00:02:12.500 --> 00:02:13.000
a villain.

00:02:13.100 --> 00:02:18.280
Not only did he impress as Mordo in the MCU,
but he also lent his gruff voice to the treacherous

00:02:18.280 --> 00:02:21.060
lion Scar in the recent remake of The Lion
King.

00:02:21.280 --> 00:02:25.000
Based on where the information is coming from,
it may be solid intel.

00:02:25.010 --> 00:02:29.200
We Got This Covered notes that the source
who provided the intel that Ejiofor is on

00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:32.590
a "wishlist" at Warner Bros. for The Batman
is the same source that dished up the info

00:02:32.590 --> 00:02:36.560
that Robert Pattinson would be playing Batman
in the new film, breaking the news before

00:02:36.560 --> 00:02:38.060
Variety confirmed it.

00:02:38.260 --> 00:02:42.230
If Ejiofor does end up signing on to portray
the Riddler in The Batman, he'll follow in

00:02:42.230 --> 00:02:46.739
the footsteps of Frank Gorshin, who played
the character on the 1960s live-action Batman

00:02:46.739 --> 00:02:52.480
series and the 1966 film Batman; John Astin,
who took on the role for one two-part episode

00:02:52.480 --> 00:02:57.150
in the second season of Batman; Cory Michael
Smith, who portrays the Riddler on Gotham;

00:02:57.150 --> 00:03:00.760
and Jim Carrey, who played the villain in
1995's Batman Forever.

00:03:00.860 --> 00:03:04.540
Director Reeves has stated that the film would
get in front of cameras around the end of

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:08.940
2019, so it's too early to say what Ejiofor's
role in the movie will be, if any.

00:03:09.020 --> 00:03:14.020
Until Warner Bros., Reeves, or Ejiofor himself
comes forward to confirm his involvement,

00:03:14.020 --> 00:03:16.720
we'll all have to cross our fingers and hope
for the best.

00:03:17.090 --> 00:03:21.120
With any luck, the decision to bring Ejiofor
aboard The Batman will be much, much simpler

00:03:21.120 --> 00:03:23.420
than any of the Riddler's wild puzzles.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:24.320
"Ho-ho!

00:03:24.460 --> 00:03:27.640
What is it that no man wants to have, yet
no man wants to lose?"

00:03:28.860 --> 00:03:29.560
"A lawsuit!"

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:33.000
The Batman is set for release June 25, 2021.

